        "text": "Informatics department comments: RESTRICTIONS: Most IN4MATX courses will be initially restricted to majors in the Donald Bren School of Information and Computer Sciences ONLY. Some courses will be additionally restricted to specific majors or level(s) of standing. For restriction details and timeline: http://ics.uci.edu/course-enrollment-restrictions/ WAITLIST: Students on the waitlist for an ICS course should be in communication with that course's instructor to arrange for access to course materials and submission of any assignments. Being on the waitlist or completing coursework DOES NOT guarantee a seat in the course. DISCUSSIONS & LABS: Discussion and lab sections begin meeting AFTER the first lecture unless otherwise specified by the course instructor. Always check for messages from your instructors before the start of instruction. Some lab sections are scheduled in laptop instructional labs ICS 364A, ICS2 162, or ICS2 170. Students enrolled in these labs are required to bring a personal laptop to class meetings. B or X Restricted Courses: Courses with a B or X restriction require an authorization code from the instructor to enroll."
